\f1\fs22 Eloise\'92s cavalcade slid out of the Ghetto, and joined the traffic on an arterial road like sharks among bait fish. They neither sped nor slowed as traffic lights and commuter fear made sure their progress out of the Pale was as steady as a wide deep river. Once over the council border, it took a slip-road towards a \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
hover-pad stalk \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 looming\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
 like a grey stand of celery, its leaves occluded in the Layer. The ground cars approached tangentially, taking a curving ramp off the public road which lead to a tunnel access. There we no boom gates or doors, no guardhouse, no apparent surveillance equipment. The only distinguishing feature of the square mouth of the tunnel, an engraved inscription in its concrete lintel: 
\fs18 SHAKTI ENTERPRISES
\fs22 . Those words were all the security needed; connoting, as they did, all kinds of threats and forewarnings. 
